`Context-dependent`. Mandatory on public API borders or network boundaries receiving untrusted data; on any path where mutation or another entry point can invalidate the assumption; and for useful invariant assertions, which are distinct from repeated branch-and-return error handling.
```rust
// Correct: trust the constructor's invariant inside the barricade,
// optionally documenting it with a diagnostic assertion
fn update_internal_profile(&self) {
    debug_assert!(!self.username.is_empty());
    db::write_profile(&self.username); // non-empty by construction
}
